  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the circuit shown, the energy stored in the capacitor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;J</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is _____.</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"assets\\qt0032_4baeecdde03c.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 142px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "75",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The capacitor works as an open circuit in the given configuration.</p><p>The potential difference between the two plates of the capacitor will be the difference across the resistors having resistances&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math>.</p><p>Hence, the potential difference&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;across the capacitor can be calculated as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>V</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The formula to calculate the energy stored in the capacitor is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>U</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>C</mi><mo>(</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></mrow></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (1) to calculate the required energy stored.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>U</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>75</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;J</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}